# Day-1 Commands — Wazuh Windows Endpoint Integration

## 01. Verify Wazuh Agent Service

Run on the Windows endpoint as Administrator:

```powershell
Get-Service WazuhSvc
```

Purpose: Verify that the Wazuh agent service is installed and running.

---

## 02. Verify Wazuh Agent Service Details

```powershell
Get-Service WazuhSvc | Format-List *
```

Purpose: Verify Wazuh agent service configuration and status.

---

## 03. Test Windows Endpoint to Wazuh Manager Connectivity

```powershell
Test-NetConnection 192.168.23.133 -Port 1514
```

Expected:

```text
TcpTestSucceeded : True
```

Purpose: Verify connectivity between the Windows endpoint and Wazuh Manager.

---

## 04. Verify Domain Secure Channel

```powershell
Test-ComputerSecureChannel -Verbose
```

Expected:

```text
True
```

Purpose: Verify the secure channel between the Windows endpoint and the
Kamran.local domain.

---

## 05. Generate a Windows Test Event

```powershell
Write-EventLog -LogName Application -Source "WazuhTest" -EventId 1001 -EntryType Information -Message "Day-1 Wazuh telemetry test from KAMRAN-PC"
```

Purpose: Generate a controlled Windows Application event for Wazuh telemetry testing.

---

## 06. Verify the Windows Test Event

```powershell
Get-WinEvent -LogName Application -MaxEvents 20 |
Where-Object {$_.ProviderName -eq "WazuhTest"}
```

Or:

```powershell
Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{
    LogName='Application'
    Id=1001
} -MaxEvents 10
```

Purpose: Confirm that the test event was successfully created on Windows.

---

## 07. Verify Wazuh Archive Collection

Run on the Wazuh Manager:

```bash
sudo grep -A5 -B2 "archives:" /etc/filebeat/filebeat.yml
```

Check the archive:

```bash
sudo ls -lh /var/ossec/logs/archives/archives.json
```

Search for the test event:

```bash
sudo grep -n "Day-1 Wazuh telemetry test from KAMRAN-PC" /var/ossec/logs/archives/archives.json
```

Or search by Event ID:

```bash
sudo grep -n '"eventID":"1001"' /var/ossec/logs/archives/archives.json
```

Purpose: Verify that Wazuh archived the Windows telemetry.

---

## 08. Verify Event in Wazuh Discover

Open Wazuh/OpenSearch Discover.

Index:

```text
wazuh-archives-*
```

Search:

```text
"Day-1 Wazuh telemetry test from KAMRAN-PC"
```

Additional searches:

```text
agent.name:"KamranAgent"
```

```text
agent.id:"001"
```

Purpose: Verify that the Windows event is searchable in Wazuh/OpenSearch.

---

## 09. Verify Filebeat Output

Run on the Wazuh Manager:

```bash
sudo filebeat test output
```

Verify Filebeat service:

```bash
sudo systemctl status filebeat --no-pager
```

Verify archive configuration:

```bash
sudo grep -A5 -B2 "archives:" /etc/filebeat/filebeat.yml
```

Purpose: Verify Filebeat connectivity to the OpenSearch/Elasticsearch-compatible endpoint and confirm that the archive configuration is enabled.
